{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Chitram is a 2000 Telugu film written and directed by Teja.","title":"Chitram"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" This film stars Uday Kiran & Reema Sen in the lead roles and marked the debut of the lead actors.","title":"Chitram"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The film was sensational hit in 2000.","title":"Chitram"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The film is produced by Ramoji Rao and has music composed by R.P. Patnaik.","title":"Chitram"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The film was released as "Chithiram" in Tamil in 2001 with the film mostly featuring scenes dubbed from the original although scenes involving Manivannan and Senthil were added.","title":"Chitram"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" "Chitram" and "Nuvve Kavali" were the two movies which set a trend of college campus romance stories in the same year.","title":"Chitram"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The movie was remade in Kannada as "Chithra", starring Prabhu Deva's brother Nagendra Prasad and Rekha Vedavyas in 2001 under the direction of Dinesh Baboo and the production of Ramoji Rao.","title":"Chitram"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" The movie was a superhit in Kannada and marked the debut of the lead actors.","title":"Chitram"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Ocean's Thirteen is a 2007 American comedy heist film directed by Steven Soderbergh and starring an ensemble cast.","title":"Ocean's Thirteen"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is the third and final film in the Soderbergh-directed "Ocean's Trilogy", following the 2004 sequel "Ocean's Twelve" and the 2001 film "Ocean's Eleven", which itself was a remake of the 1960 Rat Pack film "Ocean's 11".","title":"Ocean's Thirteen"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" All the male cast members reprise their roles from the previous installments, but neither Julia Roberts nor Catherine Zeta-Jones returns.","title":"Ocean's Thirteen"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Rat Pack is a term used by the media to refer to an informal group of entertainers centered on the Las Vegas casino scene.","title":"Rat Pack"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Having its origins in a group of friends that met at the Los Angeles home of Humphrey Bogart and Lauren Bacall, by the 1960s, it was the name used by the press and the general public to refer to a later variation of the group that called itself "the Summit" or "the Clan", featuring Frank Sinatra, Dean Martin, Sammy Davis Jr., Peter Lawford and Joey Bishop among others; they appeared together on stage and in films in the early 1960s, including the movies "Ocean's 11", "Sergeants 3", and "Robin and the 7 Hoods" (in the last film, Bing Crosby replaced Lawford).","title":"Rat Pack"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Sinatra, Martin, and Davis were regarded as the group's lead members.","title":"Rat Pack"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Khilona (English: Toy ) is a 1970 Indian drama film, produced by L.V. Prasad on Prasad Productions Pvt.Ltd.","title":"Khilona (1970 film)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" banner and directed by Chander Vohra.","title":"Khilona (1970 film)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Starring Sanjeev Kumar, Mumtaz, Jeetendra in lead roles.","title":"Khilona (1970 film)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Other actors in supporting roles are Shatrughan Sinha, Durga Khote, Ramesh Deo, Jagdeep and music composed by Laxmikant-Pyarelal.","title":"Khilona (1970 film)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The film recorded as "Super Hit" at the box office.","title":"Khilona (1970 film)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The film was a remake of Telugu film "Punarjanma".","title":"Khilona (1970 film)"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The film was not remade in Tamil instead both Hindi and Tamil version were simultaneously made.","title":"Khilona (1970 film)"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Tamil version had "Engirundho Vandhaal" with Sivaji Ganesan and Jayalalithaa.","title":"Khilona (1970 film)"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" The film was also remade in Malayalam as "Amrithavaahini".","title":"Khilona (1970 film)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Bad Animals is the ninth studio album by the American rock band Heart, released on June 6, 1987 by Capitol Records.","title":"Bad Animals"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The album continues the mainstream hard rock style from the band's 1985 self-titled release, all while enjoying similar success.","title":"Bad Animals"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" RIAA certification as of 1992 is three times platinum, indicating sales in excess of three million copies in the US alone.","title":"Bad Animals"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The album reached No. 2 on the U.S. "Billboard" 200 chart in August 1987.","title":"Bad Animals"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" "Bad Animals" contained the number one hit single "Alone", while "Who Will You Run To" reached No. 7, "There's the Girl" reached No. 12, and "I Want You So Bad" reached No. 49.","title":"Bad Animals"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The album is notable for containing only a few tracks with writing contributions from lead members Ann and Nancy Wilson.","title":"Bad Animals"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" It received a Grammy nomination for Best Rock Performance by a Duo or Group with Vocal.","title":"Bad Animals"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Marc Barthel (also known as Jesse D'Lane) is a singer, actor, songwriter and dubbing actor from Berlin, Germany.","title":"Marc Barthel"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He was born on Oct. 04, 1989 in Berlin and first became famous as one of the lead members of the pop group ''.","title":"Marc Barthel"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He left the group in 2007 to focus on his solo music career as 'Jesse D'Lane'.","title":"Marc Barthel"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Furthermore, he has since then been working as an actor in television, film and commercial productions.","title":"Marc Barthel"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Frank Sinatra, Dean Martin, Sammy Davis Jr.
